2. SOURCE CODE TERMS
==============================================================================
The Author makes the Source Code publicly available under the following terms:

(a) PERMITTED USES FOR INDIVIDUALS & NON-PROFIT ENTITIES:
    Individuals (acting solely for private and non-commercial purposes), students,
    educational institutions, and non-profit organizations are granted a non-exclusive,
    worldwide, royalty-free license to:
    1. Inspect, audit, and view the Source Code for security review, transparency,
       and educational learning.
    2. Modify, adapt, and build the Source Code locally for private, internal,
       educational, and personal research, debugging, and experimentation.
    3. Fork the repository solely for the purpose of creating and submitting
       bug fixes, enhancements, or Pull Requests (PRs) back to the official
       upstream repository (https://github.com/smin987/ImageOptimizer).

(b) COMMERCIAL ENTITY TERMS: AUDIT PERMITTED, MODIFICATION STRICTLY PROHIBITED:
    Commercial Entities and for-profit businesses are granted the right to inspect,
    view, and audit the Source Code strictly for security, safety, and compatibility
    verification purposes. However:
    1. MODIFICATION STRICTLY PROHIBITED: Commercial Entities are STRICTLY PROHIBITED
       from modifying, altering, adapting, patching, or creating derivative works of
       the Source Code for internal or external use.
    2. CUSTOM BUILDS PROHIBITED: Commercial Entities may not compile or build custom
       binaries for deployment or internal workflow automation.
    3. OFFICIAL BINARIES USE: Commercial Entities are fully permitted and encouraged
       to install, execute, and deploy the official Compiled Binaries free of charge
       in accordance with Section 3.

(c) PROHIBITION ON PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION OF MODIFIED VERSIONS:
    You may NOT publicly distribute, publish, host, mirror, or make available
    to third parties any modified versions, patches, forks, or derivative works
    of the Source Code without the Author's explicit prior written consent.

(d) PROHIBITION ON COMPETING PRODUCTS & MODIFICATIONS FOR COMPETITION:
    Modifying the Source Code to develop, build, or release a Competing Product
    is strictly prohibited. You may NOT use the Source Code, in whole or in part,
    modified or unmodified, to build, market, distribute, or license any Competing
    Product or service, whether offered for free or for a fee.
    Provided, however, that third-party open-source components incorporated in or
    used by this Software remain subject to their respective license notices and terms.

(e) PROHIBITION ON REDISTRIBUTION & RESALE:
    You may NOT sublicense, lease, rent, sell, or commercialize the Source Code
    in any manner.

